the Sun (represented by the radius of their orbits) and the semi-major axis of the ellipse is illustrated by the two circles being drawn with their radii proportional to the semi-axis, as indicated by the scale at the bottom right.\n>\n> In the context of the document, this diagram serves as a visual aid to explain Kepler's laws of planetary motion and the concept of escape speed in the context of satellites orbiting Earth. The reference to Tycho Brahe suggests that his observations were critical in the development of these theories.", chunk_id:"971f150dfa3f5170c09ef0015a38ce21", next_chunk_id:"8630acf6b41df6b46461d0b7f501a126"}}, {_id:777, properties:{text_embedding:[-0.03711376711726189, 0.027430618181824684, -0.009934254921972752, 0.019236788153648376, -0.027144882827997208, -0.0423051081597805, -0.04810406267642975, -0.031246809288859367, 0.028902634978294373, -0.009568193927407265, -0.011066834442317486, 0.04303296282887459, -0.053648099303245544, 7.140369270928204E-4, 0.004944637417793274, 0.05891592800617218, 0.033267054706811905, -0.004741114564239979, 0.020211413502693176, -0.0016771736554801464, 0.005211439915001392, -0.012373028323054314, 0.024920372292399406, -0.001176477991975844, -0.0021509609650820494, 0.01900780014693737, 0.010957600548863411, 0.020804958418011665, -0.02895389311015606, 0.005852638278156519, -0.013976691290736198, -0.033852629363536835, 0.026045987382531166, 0.018891796469688416, -0.021618865430355072, -0.008958952501416206, 0.032824717462062836, -0.02680293284356594, -0.04895411431789398, -0.01760486513376236, -0.0025190652813762426, -0.020593317225575447, 0.018007513135671616, -0.05342236906290054, 0.04480764642357826, -0.03833141550421715, -0.04507836699485779, -0.03234840929508209, -0.024464808404445648, -0.032927967607975006, 0.006712198257446289, -0.0012480643345043063, 0.06251949816942215, 0.022953150793910027, -0.0037323562428355217, 0.0017071773763746023, 0.013033447787165642, -0.04457243159413338, -0.008620436303317547, -0.