V_p = m_p r_A V_A$$  \nor\n$$\\frac{v_p}{v_A} = \\frac{r_A}{r_p}$$  \nThe area  $SBAC$  bounded by the ellipse and the radius vectors  $SB$  and  $SC$  is larger than  $SBPC$  in Fig. 7.1. From Kepler's second law, equal areas are swept in equal times. Hence the planet will take a longer time to traverse  $BAC$  than  $CPB$ .", chunk_id:"9cbfc6ec760700862326a049fd20ceb3", next_chunk_id:"68cf5f539ca5a529f5c29267df19f515"}}] AS row
