ntered around a point mass m. The shell is shown in a top-down view, with a line indicating a depth below the surface.\n>\n> The surrounding document text provides mathematical equations related to gravitational forces exerted by these spheres on the point mass. The equations involve the mass of the smaller sphere (Ms) and its radius (RE - d), which is smaller than that of the larger shell (RE).\n>\n> Equation (7.16) relates the force exerted due to the outer shell (R_E) and the spherical shell of thickness d, stating that it is as if all the mass in this shell is concentrated at the center. The equation also mentions a result in the previous section but does not detail its content within the context provided.\n>", chunk_id:"a40309e051545477471abfad40e02636", next_chunk_id:"62dbe1def56e6b9da8dc1cc6640f9a80"}}, {_id:819, properties:{text_embedding:[0.014673379249870777, 0.04768673703074455, -0.02177027426660061, -0.04719819501042366, -0.007819227874279022, -0.02629854343831539, 0.006331579759716988, 0.02838190272450447, 0.04453210160136223, -0.015804393216967583, -0.0172832440584898, 0.011837723664939404, -0.04139367491006851, 0.008173833601176739, -0.03101217746734619, 0.011126267723739147, 0.0248244758695364, 0.029589276760816574, 6.465022452175617E-4, 0.006425357889384031, 0.01343309786170721, 0.025641165673732758, -0.021199317649006844, -0.02302849292755127, 0.03184199333190918, 0.04979843273758888, 0.01572434790432453, 0.017526889219880104, 0.025430738925933838, 0.020664149895310402, -0.002357983263209462, -0.023033883422613144, -0.0024891127832233906, -0.036190032958984375, 0.005404585972428322, -0.0024719161447137594, -0.03491521254181862, -0.02056857757270336, -0.03942602872848511, 0.0183180570602417, -0.044494349509477615, 0.0022831421811133623, 0.05623447895050049, -0.04520382732152939, 0.029117759317159653, -0.048304710537195206, -0.01456642709672451, -0.03659806773066521, -0.06238490343093872, -0.028977546840906143, 0.004439019598066807, -0.01391183957457