7)$$  \nSubstituting for  $M_s$  from above, we get  \n$$F(d) = G M_E m (R_E - d) / R_E^3 \\quad (7.18)$$  \nand hence the acceleration due to gravity at a depth  $d$ ,  \n$$\\begin{aligned} g(d) &= \\frac{F(d)}{m} \\text{ is} \\\\ g(d) &= \\frac{F(d)}{m} = \\frac{GM_E}{R_E^3} (R_E - d) \\\\ &= g \\frac{R_E - d}{R_E} = g(1 - d/R_E) \\end{aligned} \\quad (7.19)$$  \nThus, as we go down below earth's surface, the acceleration due gravity decreases by a factor  $(1 - d/R_E)$ . The remarkable thing about acceleration due to earth's gravity is that it is maximum on its surface decreasing whether you go up or down.  \n**7.7 GRAVITATIONAL POTENTIAL ENERGY**", chunk_id:"221d8f824ef39f375e7079ca2fd88378", next_chunk_id:"e8754dff562e50e2a2fa8f5031c73c36"}}, {_id:823, properties:{text_embedding:[0.006229714956134558, 0.03108048625290394, -0.0030859012622386217, 0.0067837657406926155, -0.0026535075157880783, -0.09588630497455597, 0.0059767719358205795, 0.04190126433968544, 0.04120993614196777, -0.025790100917220116, -0.02571970969438553, -0.014476204290986061, -0.05677499994635582, -0.009152359329164028, -0.013454304076731205, 0.033420659601688385, 0.007385564967989922, 0.011012677103281021, -0.018144963309168816, -0.001990667777135968, 0.014985407702624798, -0.01318760123103857, 0.019138090312480927, 0.0386069118976593, 0.01756373979151249, 0.020644960924983025, -0.015001107938587666, 0.006718670483678579, 0.01617358811199665, 0.025251204147934914, 0.002838423941284418, 0.004423888400197029, 0.0015754286432638764, -0.047438591718673706, 0.01932920515537262, 0.00968743022531271, -0.006529082078486681, -0.04717148840427399, -0.004563131369650364, 0.03922297805547714, 0.006287095136940479, -0.05650494620203972, 0.043023932725191116, -0.03314080461859703, -0.006927103735506535, -0.0329316109418869, -0.042248550802469254, -0.03229963034391403, -0.02598731406033039, -0.055398356169462204, -0.003798170480877161, -0.04073124751448631, 0.05110936239361763, 0.005426708143204451, -0.0229