dy by the force. As we had discussed earlier, forces for which the work done is independent of the path are the conservative forces.  \nThe force of gravity is a conservative force and we can calculate the potential energy of a body arising out of this force, called the gravitational potential energy. Consider points", chunk_id:"e8754dff562e50e2a2fa8f5031c73c36", next_chunk_id:"7c40997f79515711ba6d0a31b647b787"}}, {_id:824, properties:{text_embedding:[0.011571280658245087, 0.018822908401489258, -0.010720943100750446, -0.011605209670960903, 8.4545963909477E-4, -0.05673051252961159, 0.049799058586359024, 0.03330985829234123, 0.003800156991928816, -0.0031925486400723457, -0.03615906462073326, 0.0028801115695387125, -0.016112659126520157, -0.001842941390350461, 0.02404920384287834, 0.043847523629665375, 0.02011701464653015, -0.0011791838333010674, 0.022939220070838928, 0.035784363746643066, -0.032641101628541946, -0.0035547863226383924, -7.555808406323195E-4, 0.019152550026774406, -0.017274798825383186, 0.044899988919496536, -0.008122565224766731, 0.015424218960106373, 0.025499846786260605, 0.05602259188890457, -0.01654881052672863, -0.049951646476984024, 0.005304819904267788, -0.032185886055231094, 0.0010616814251989126, 0.01770048402249813, -0.02152913436293602, -0.017137590795755386, -0.03846573084592819, -0.003613881068304181, -0.03733203932642937, -0.04538276791572571, 0.022292325273156166, -0.011355720460414886, 0.006483201868832111, -0.0354953333735466, -0.04827413335442543, -0.05166022479534149, -0.05133320763707161, -0.050693050026893616, -0.04737289622426033, -0.04232817888259888, 0.06491430103778839, 0.012950737029314041, -0.005178908351808786, -0.013868317939341068, -0.05931227654218674, -0.033499203622341156, -0.04585828259587288, -0.021139301359653473, 0.00576756102964282, 0.04580506309866905, -0.04145647585391998, -0.027466554194688797, -0.009874626062810421, 0.002310661133378744, -0.01029896643012762, 0.02509123459458351, -0.022884000092744827, -0.037010