e of mass *M* directly towards the centre of the second sphere. Obtain an expression for the minimum speed v of the projectile so that it reaches the surface of the second sphere.  \n*Fig. 7.10*  \n*Answer* The projectile is acted upon by two mutually opposing gravitational forces of the two spheres. The neutral point N (see Fig. 7.10) is defined as the position where the two forces cancel each other exactly. If ON = *r*, we have  \n$$\\frac{G M m}{r^2} = \\frac{4 G M m}{(6R-r)^2}$$  \n$$(6R-r)^2 = 4r^2$$  \n$$6R - r = \\pm 2r$$  \n$$r = 2R \\quad \\text{or} \\quad -6R.$$", chunk_id:"81ec8ec2e0994f43807a25f71f5090bb", next_chunk_id:"e5a30dddd31fac8c6434faf78b86fc7f"}}, {_id:839, properties:{text_embedding:[-0.02313496544957161, 0.0038558540400117636, 0.05770525336265564, -0.021368179470300674, -0.00575336953625083, -0.030628729611635208, 0.01661643199622631, -0.001139918458648026, -0.010119468905031681, 0.012758158147335052, -0.014903935603797436, 0.003883143188431859, -0.0057096402160823345, -0.004143562633544207, 0.03163367137312889, 0.02582511678338051, -0.0018650991842150688, 0.06469787657260895, 0.015270371921360493, -0.01749778352677822, 0.017651064321398735, -0.01607660762965679, -0.02419188991189003, 0.01695275865495205, 0.014408745802938938, -0.0010496496688574553, -0.01732541248202324, -6.492203683592379E-4, 0.007158401422202587, 0.05498357117176056, -0.034599948674440384, -0.04297350347042084, -0.010323832742869854, -0.0660332664847374, -0.01972065307199955, 0.00899455789476633, -0.019148612394928932, -0.01996641978621483, -0.029557272791862488, 0.03506327420473099, 0.00457399245351553, -0.045333195477724075, 0.039618268609046936, -0.018489964306354523, 0.03018423169851303, -0.0394430086016655, -0.03882012143731117, -0.03754238784313202, -0.00343150133267045, -0.06436479091644287, -0.03736220300197601, -0.03760996088385582, 0.038724884390830994, -0.02506609447300434, -0.0030281657818704844, 0.005711646284908056, -0.017645150423049927, 0.005701042711734772