we get  \n$$T_0 = 2\\pi\\sqrt{\\frac{6.4 \\times 10^6}{9.8}} \\text{ s}$$  \nWhich is approximately 85 minutes.  \n**Answer** (i) We employ Eq. (7.38) with the Sun's mass replaced by the martian mass *M<sup>m</sup>*  \n$$T^2 = \\frac{4\\pi^2}{GM_{\\text{B}^2}} R^3$$", chunk_id:"9e1fd53e60727bffa8b724cffd23258d", next_chunk_id:"c828fd930ddaff3ccbbb54b39c7386b0"}}, {_id:844, properties:{text_embedding:[0.008160696364939213, 0.041435230523347855, -0.015566257759928703, 0.009018045850098133, -0.02417534403502941, -0.06526919454336166, -0.01276416052132845, -0.006726242136210203, -0.01817753165960312, 0.017028409987688065, -0.07044093310832977, 0.00729750981554389, -0.005109996534883976, -0.00544241676107049, 0.005742704030126333, 0.020101215690374374, 0.005245508626103401, 0.028150008991360664, 0.002615704433992505, -0.037083569914102554, -0.008210701867938042, 0.04061850160360336, -0.008332740515470505, 0.003122073831036687, -0.004872428718954325, 0.019831759855151176, -0.010545728728175163, 9.392812353326008E-5, 0.043686289340257645, 0.035282984375953674, -0.021097740158438683, -0.022606536746025085, 0.010858168825507164, -0.07657771557569504, -0.019889364019036293, 0.007340176030993462, -0.02499309368431568, 0.012428244575858116, -0.04753473773598671, -0.007474793121218681, -0.040901605039834976, -0.04178352281451225, 0.02110772579908371, -0.02663402631878853, 0.06318358331918716, -0.042541440576314926, -0.019606251269578934, -0.04892799258232117, 0.01432016957551241, -0.056311216205358505, 0.012671126052737236, 0.008592160418629646, 0.05185643956065178, -0.019612573087215424, 0.004791647661477327, 0.006455008406192064, -0.033564869314432144, -0.002898700535297394, -0.04629768058657646, -0.01899823360145092, -0.03826228901743889, 0.05794180929660797, -0.0298512801527977, 0.03130680322647095, -0.008861837908625603, 0.0364103801548481, 0.01942908577620983, -0.039091650396585464, -0.009596714749932289, -0.031152503564953804, -0.026566728949546814, 0.027251852676272392, 