tential energy between two points  $r_2$  and  $r_1$  distance away from the centre of the earth.  \n7.3 Suppose there existed a planet that went around the Sun twice as fast as the earth. What would be its orbital size as compared to that of the earth ?  \n7.4 Io, one of the satellites of Jupiter, has an orbital period of 1.769 days and the radius of the orbit is  $4.22 \\times 10^8$  m. Show that the mass of Jupiter is about one-thousandth that of the sun.", chunk_id:"5f35f428d543726fb4cf2bd31e62eeeb", next_chunk_id:"6e7cf8fa274cc75e4aed46808f0b549c"}}, {_id:862, properties:{text_embedding:[0.004208889324218035, 0.019961131736636162, -0.005280680023133755, -1.8148553499486297E-4, 0.0021119550801813602, -0.033946190029382706, -0.005866103805601597, -0.02775241620838642, 0.017023447901010513, -0.009641791693866253, -0.01827624812722206, 0.0321890190243721, -0.010488273575901985, -0.024388819932937622, -0.012878102250397205, 0.0064013940282166, -0.0037219678051769733, 0.030251825228333473, 0.031209245324134827, 0.02860633283853531, -0.00814261008054018, 0.004429530818015337, 0.02000083029270172, -0.005853485781699419, 0.05555645748972893, 0.011149895377457142, -0.011621817015111446, 0.03152996674180031, 0.007188784424215555, 0.028451908379793167, -0.030418189242482185, -0.03537147864699364, 0.00843784213066101, -0.04157433658838272, 7.311098161153495E-4, -0.010112441144883633, -0.016380632296204567, -0.006442663725465536, -0.020038969814777374, 0.01765843853354454, -0.03234478458762169, -0.03663647919893265, 0.025598598644137383, -0.033782877027988434, -0.013344794511795044, -0.04605652019381523, -0.008361457847058773, -0.04155688360333443, -0.06159115582704544, -0.031082455068826675, 0.025965267792344093, -0.02243218757212162, 0.0068599386140704155, -0.014253306202590466, -0.022609565407037735, 0.03003888577222824, -0.021605635061860085, -0.016657937318086624, -0.01214440818876028, 0.001707269111648202, -0.04507822170853615, 0.03226907551288605, -0.03781397268176079